So I want to add multiple new special artifact abilities in
'artifact.h' but there seems to only be one unique position left in
the SPFX bitfield:

#define SPFX_DALIGN 0x1000000L	/* attack bonus on non-aligned
monsters  */
#define SPFX_DBONUS 0x1F00000L	/* attack bonus mask */
#define SPFX_XRAY   0x2000000L	/* gives X-RAY vision to player */
#define SPFX_REFLECT 0x4000000L /* Reflection */
#define SPFX_MY_PROP 0x8000000L	/* Last position? */

I notice, though, that only seven hex positions are being used (28
bits) and that immediately following this, spfx is declared as an
unsigned long:

struct artifact {
	short	    otyp;
	const char  *name;
	unsigned long spfx;	/* special effect from wielding/wearing */
	...

On my machine at least, spfx should then have 32 bits and therefore
four more places to stuff special flags, right? It seems to work for
me, but I am wondering if there's some portability thing that I'm not
thinking about, or some Nethack quirk that caused the Devteam to
restrict the SPFX bitfield to 28 bits?

